{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AYjzQZ5hee47RqKvkY1tMw","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-TtZ4jK/README.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12174175-2dd2-4890-b691-e715b87a072e","uuid":"7e60c94c-9085-4776-acae-1b58c381265d","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:16:07.434Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-TtZ4jK/README.md","oldString":"Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","newString":"Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on. The system\nprompt is three blocks: instructions, the athlete's profile (cached, with the one\n`cache_control` marker), and the date plus long-term facts (uncached, after the\nmarker). A `save_fact` therefore does not evict the cached prefix. Tool-loop rounds and\nfollow-up messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","originalFile":"# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":6,"newStart":11,"newLines":8,"lines":[" Run it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type"," messages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs"," `COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).","-Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system","-prompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up","-messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","+Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on. The system","+prompt is three blocks: instructions, the athlete's profile (cached, with the one","+`cache_control` marker), and the date plus long-term facts (uncached, after the","+marker). A `save_fact` therefore does not evict the cached prefix. Tool-loop rounds and","+follow-up messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AYjzQZ5hee47RqKvkY1tMw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
